      "text": "Nominal RLHF maximizes J\u02c6r(\u03c0), often with KL or clipping controls inherited from\nPPO-style training [Schulman et al., 2017]. Our algorithms do not add an explicit KL\npenalty to the policy objective: the robust correction changes the reward signal rather\nthan merely restricting optimization of the same proxy. KL reappears only as a drift\nstatistic for calibrating the dynamic ambiguity budget; Section C gives more detail.\n",
